  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What each judge sees, and does not",
      "items": [
        "Sees: the brief prompts/jury.md, the race context (redacted), the subject, the calibration example if given, and one team's file",
        "Never sees: another judge's verdict, the team's name, provider or model, identities.json",
        "Never grades its own provider's team: that pair is not in the work list",
        "Each pair is its own call, run in parallel (6 workers); a failed judge is recorded and the others still count"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Budget and failures",
      "items": [
        "Every judge call, a retry included, is reserved and charged in the jury's own ledger under --cap-usd (agent judge:<provider>)",
        "A file in which a name is still found is written to files/ but sent to no judge",
        "No report and no record: graded 0; work every judge failed on: not graded",
        "An altered ledger disqualifies: final score 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not implemented yet: grading the snapshots during the race",
      "items": [
        "The dashboard reads <root>/jury/snapshots.json (grades per snapshot commit) and jury/events.jsonl, events \"verdict\"",
        "Today only tools/fake_race.py writes them; frontier/jury.py grades once, after the race",
        "See frontier/dashboard.py, its docstring and jury_state"
      ]
    }
  ]
}